\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The evidence ladder: three levels of claim, three kinds of warrant.} \textbf  {A} is \textbf  {a general structural result}, holding by the design's structure, which no experiment could establish or refute; \textbf  {B} is \textbf  {one empirical demonstration} that the canonical black-box benchmark instantiates it, the confound being \emph  {active}; \textbf  {C} is \textbf  {a survey} of what public corpora do and do not supply---attribution, which criterion~4 alone tests (Table~\ref {tab:criteria}), and there the verdict is instrument-specific. \textbf  {Bold rows are load-bearing}; the factorial is a \emph  {diagnostic}, and sizes what is unattributable rather than attributing it.}}{3}{table.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
