\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {The protocol applied across settings: three detector paradigms, two corpora, five distinct failure modes.} Columns are Table~\ref {tab:criteria}'s criteria---\textbf  {1}~equalization, \textbf  {2}~cross-family extraction, \textbf  {3}~matched surface baseline (with $E$ fixed this also bounds \emph  {knowledge conflict}), \textbf  {4}~deception at fixed elicitation, \textbf  {5}~transfer. \text  {$\mathsurround \z@ \mathchar "458$}~passes; $\times $~fails; \textbf  {---}~not expressible by the design or not applicable to the instrument; \text  {$\mathsurround \z@ \mathchar "458$}$^{\dagger }$~criterion~4 runs and is \emph  {positive}, but requirement~(iii) is unmet, so what is established is a deception-\emph  {associated} signal, not $\tau _D$. \textbf  {Criterion~4 asks about a \emph  {design}}, and the rollout sets are \textbf  {not independent benchmark efforts}: seven designs from one release, every rollout Llama-70B (all ten: Table~\ref {tab:external_eligibility}; a second release we pre-registered and could not obtain: Appendix~\ref {app:liars_bench}).}}{8}{table.caption.20}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:external_audit}{{3}{8}{\textbf {The protocol applied across settings: three detector paradigms, two corpora, five distinct failure modes.} Columns are Table~\ref {tab:criteria}'s criteria---\textbf {1}~equalization, \textbf {2}~cross-family extraction, \textbf {3}~matched surface baseline (with $E$ fixed this also bounds \emph {knowledge conflict}), \textbf {4}~deception at fixed elicitation, \textbf {5}~transfer. \checkmark ~passes; $\times $~fails; \textbf {---}~not expressible by the design or not applicable to the instrument; \checkmark $^{\dagger }$~criterion~4 runs and is \emph {positive}, but requirement~(iii) is unmet, so what is established is a deception-\emph {associated} signal, not $\tau _D$. \textbf {Criterion~4 asks about a \emph {design}}, and the rollout sets are \textbf {not independent benchmark efforts}: seven designs from one release, every rollout Llama-70B (all ten: Table~\ref {tab:external_eligibility}; a second release we pre-registered and could not obtain: Appendix~\ref {app:liars_bench})}{table.caption.20}{}}
